      "message": "Let\u0027s use `struct`s for all data transfers. Here is Gemini-generated code to fix it. Review for correctness:\n\n----\n\n**The Rationale:** Currently, both of these functions take the raw `std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e` response from the USB transfer and use `reinterpret_cast` to overlay a typed struct pointer (`BootromInfoResponse` or `FlashInfoResponse`). This violates C++ strict aliasing rules. We will replace this with the standard-compliant `ReadStruct` helper to safely copy the bytes into local, typed structs.\n\n**The Implementation (`bootrom.cc`):**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::GetBootromInfo() {\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e cmd \u003d {EgisBootrom::kCmdGetBootInfo};\n  auto resp \u003d SendBootromCommand(cmd);\n  if (!resp) return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n\n  // Safely extract the response using ReadStruct\n  auto info_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse\u003e(*resp);\n  if (!info_res) {\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  }\n  \n  EgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse info \u003d info_res.value();\n\n  std::println(\"Bootrom Version: 0x{:x}\", FromLittleEndian(info.version));\n  std::println(\"Max Command Size: {} bytes\", FromLittleEndian(info.max_cmd_size));\n  std::println(\"Max FW Upgrade Size: {} bytes\", FromLittleEndian(info.max_fw_upgrade_size));\n  \n  return {};\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::GetFlashInfo() {\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e cmd \u003d {EgisBootrom::kCmdFlashInfo};\n  std::println(\"--- Fetching Flash Information ---\");\n\n  auto resp \u003d SendBootromCommand(cmd);\n  if (!resp) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Unable to retrieve Flash info.\");\n    return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n  }\n\n  // Safely extract the response using ReadStruct\n  auto info_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEgisBootrom::FlashInfoResponse\u003e(*resp);\n  if (!info_res) {\n    std::println(stderr